1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,500
This bundle has a Lightning cable, but my phone uses USB-C.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:12,500
So the store refuses to take my money, and takes me straight to the reason and the fix.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:19,500
OpenHands Commerce: an accessible shopping assistant that checks your order before PayPal opens.

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:38,500
I describe what I need in my own words, using only the keyboard. Claude reads my request and works out what I'm shopping for.

5
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:46,500
Claude writes the explanations, and the label says so. Every price and stock fact comes from our catalog.

6
00:00:46,500 --> 00:01:09,500
I pick the bundle with the wrong cable. Our rules find the problem, Claude explains it, and the fix is the next stop. One key, same price, and the total, $40.62 with shipping and tax, is within my budget.

7
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Our server decides what's safe to buy. Claude has no tools and can't touch money, and everything it writes is checked against the order before you see it.

8
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:30,500
PayPal creates an order bound to that exact quote. I confirm in PayPal Sandbox. It's test money only.

9
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:51,500
We capture once, then ask PayPal directly. The receipt says paid only when PayPal reports the capture as completed, for the amount I approved.

10
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:55,500
If I cancel, nothing is charged and my order is kept.

11
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,300
It works in high-contrast mode…

12
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:07,300
…at 400 percent zoom, and with the keyboard alone.

13
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:18,300
OpenHands Commerce. Claude explains, our rules decide, and you stay in control.
